{"id":28056,"slug":"rosetta","title":"Rosetta","year":1999,"country":"Belgium","duration":93,"spine":621,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28056-rosetta","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/06eeae01a332a952d5c2bb0c8c5ecc78/wB6ANgwbN29LKWFvsvDzs0NEvkfbmP_large.jpg","description":"The Belgian filmmaking team of brothers Luc and Jean-Pierre Dardenne turned heads with Rosetta, an intense vérité drama that closely follows a poor young woman struggling to hold on to a job to support herself and her alcoholic mother. It’s a swift and simple tale made revelatory by the raw, empathetic way in which the directors render Rosetta’s desperation, keeping the camera nearly perched on her shoulder throughout. Many have copied the Dardennes’ style, but few have equaled it. This ferocious film won big at Cannes, earning the Palme d’Or for the filmmakers and the best actress prize for the indomitable Émilie Dequenne.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Luc Dardenne","slug":"luc-dardenne"},{"name":"Jean-Pierre Dardenne","slug":"jean-pierre-dardenne"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Emilie Dequenne","role":"Rosetta","slug":"emilie-dequenne"},{"actor":"Fabrizio Rongione","role":"Riquet","slug":"fabrizio-rongione"},{"actor":"Anne Yernaux","role":"Mother","slug":"anne-yernaux"},{"actor":"Olivier Gourmet","role":"Boss","slug":"olivier-gourmet"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Luc Dardenne","slug":"luc-dardenne"},{"role":"Director","person":"Jean-Pierre Dardenne","slug":"jean-pierre-dardenne"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Luc Dardenne","slug":"luc-dardenne"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Jean-Pierre Dardenne","slug":"jean-pierre-dardenne"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Luc Dardenne","slug":"luc-dardenne"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Jean-Pierre Dardenne","slug":"jean-pierre-dardenne"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Michèle Pétin","slug":null},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Laurent Pétin","slug":null},{"role":"First assistant director","person":"